WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:11.939
You have to make sure you have a robust change management process and make sure you

2
00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:14.600
test in model environments before you make any

3
00:00:14.609 --> 00:00:17.069
change in a production or live environment.

4
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.780
Even with extensive planning and testing,

5
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:22.420
there are sometimes unintended consequences.

6
00:00:22.549 --> 00:00:25.190
So you must make sure there is a rollback plan.

7
00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:28.030
A rollback is restoring the system to the state.

8
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.209
It was in before the change was made to

9
00:00:30.219 --> 00:00:32.560
the point where we know it was working properly.

10
00:00:32.569 --> 00:00:34.909
Before we introduce changes into the environment,

11
00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:38.229
we need to make sure we review and test

12
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.270
all the patches and can restore the previous configuration.

13
00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:44.599
Maintaining a separate testing environment can

14
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:47.430
be a logistical challenge for many organizations

15
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.319
as such.

16
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.509
Many do not have separate production and testing environments

17
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.419
to properly vet all patches and system updates.

18
00:00:55.069 --> 00:00:55.849
In this case,

19
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.630
they may rely on vendor third party testing to certify a

20
00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:01.479
new software released based on a generic set of data.

21
00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:04.919
The rollback plan is important in all environments

22
00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:09.639
but it is absolutely critical in those who are unable to fully test a change.